    {
      "kind": "text",
      "content": "Scientists tell us that there are about 120 000 000 000 stars in our galaxy, the Milky Way. Only the first two digits in this number are significant, the zeros are place holders to show the position of the decimal point.\n\nLarge numbers like this are awkward to write and difficult to read. To express very large numbers (and very small numbers) more simply, we use **__scientific notation__**.\n\nWhen a number is expressed in scientific notation, it is written as a product of:\n- A number greater than or equal to 1 but less than 10, and\n- A power of 10"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "content": "That is, $120\\,000\\,000\\,000 =$ [[box: 1.2]] $\\times\\ 10$[[box-sup: 11]]\n\n$0.000\\,000\\,000\\,000\\,000\\,000\\,000\\,001\\,67 =$ [[box: 1.67]] $\\times\\ 10$[[box-sup: -24]]"
    },
    {
      "kind": "example",
      "prompt": "Simplify\n$$\\frac{24\\,000\\,000\\,000 \\times 0.00002}{3200} =$$",
      "space": 7
    },
    {
      "kind": "example",
      "prompt": "Write in scientific notation and estimate the answer to one significant digit\n$$\\frac{389527 \\times 6058732}{4793.82} =$$\n$389527 \\doteq 4 \\times 10^5$\n$6058732 \\doteq 6 \\times 10^6$\n$4793.82 \\doteq 5 \\times 10^3$",
      "space": 4
    },
    {
      "kind": "pageBreak"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Powers of Ten and Zero exponent",
      "align": "center",
      "size": "m"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "content": "$10^{7} =$ [[line-s: $10\\,000\\,000$]]\n$10^{6} =$ [[line-s: $1\\,000\\,000$]]\n$10^{5} =$ [[line-s: $100\\,000$]]\n$10^{4} =$ [[line-s: $10\\,000$]]\n$10^{3} =$ [[line-s: $1000$]]\n$10^{2} =$ [[line-s: $100$]]\n$10^{1} =$ [[line-s: $10$]]\n$10^{0} =$ [[line-s: $1$]]\n$10^{-1} =$ [[line-s: $0.1$]]\n$10^{-2} =$ [[line-s: $0.01$]]\n$10^{-3} =$ [[line-s: $0.001$]]"
    },
